        <paragraph spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">ADA Ch. 1 Definitions</paragraph>
        <paragraph spacingafter="4" level="1" />
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" level="1" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Wall_beginbridge_ht=23.4266 ft">
                <expbody>Wall_beginbridge_ht=23.4266 ft</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Entered wall-top height used in the begin-bridge ramp notes.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_015_Wall_beginbridge_ht" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is the height recorded for the top of the MSE wall at the beginning of the bridge. It is an input to the geometry discussion. The 5 percent ramp-length equation below contains its own fixed rise value rather than a live reference to this variable.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" level="1" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45=4.46 ft">
                <expbody>Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45=4.46 ft</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Vertical distance from the slab top to the bottom of the exterior FIB45 beam.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_016_Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This entered depth follows the name of the exterior-beam geometry used in this clearance note. Subtract it from the slab-top-to-terrain distance to obtain the space remaining below the beam. It is a vertical offset, not a ground elevation.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" level="1" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="VerticalClearance=BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Distance_Algn2Terrain-Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45 to ft">
                <expbody>VerticalClearance=BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Distance_Algn2Terrain-Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45 to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 18.211 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Clear vertical space from the exterior beam bottom down to the terrain.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_017_VerticalClearance" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                <dynexp formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Distance_Algn2Terrain" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Distance_Algn2Terrain</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                 is the full vertical distance from the slab top to the terrain. Subtract 
                <dynexp formula="Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Distance_topSlab_btExtFIB45</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the depth occupied above the exterior beam bottom. The remaining distance is the under-beam clearance for these entered geometries; “to ft” displays it in feet.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="4" level="1" />
        <paragraph spacingafter="4" level="1" />
        <paragraph spacingafter="4" level="1">
            <image source="Resource11" width="175.14036901498008" height="235.48666196573748" />
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Length_req_5p=(23.4266 ft-9 in)/0.05">
                <expbody>Length_req_5p=(23.4266 ft-9 in)/0.05</expbody>
                <expresult> = 453 ft 6.384 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Horizontal sloping-run length needed for the entered rise at a 5 percent grade.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_018_Length_req_5p" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" level="1">Subtract the fixed 9 in allowance from the fixed 23.4266 ft rise in this expression. Divide the remaining vertical rise by 0.05, which means 0.05 ft of rise for each horizontal foot of run.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">Dividing by the slope converts a vertical height change into a horizontal run. This equation does not add separate level landing lengths. Its fixed rise value is not linked to the wall-height variable above.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Option_1=Length_req_5p-447.8174 ft">
                <expbody>Option_1=Length_req_5p-447.8174 ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 5 ft 8.575 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Remaining run-length difference for ramp layout option 1.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_019_Option_1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                <dynexp formula="Length_req_5p" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Length_req_5p</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                 is the required horizontal sloping run at 5 percent. Subtract the 447.8174 ft length entered for this layout option. A positive result means the option is short by that distance; a negative result means the entered option length exceeds the calculated run requirement.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Option_2=Length_req_5p-460.64 ft">
                <expbody>Option_2=Length_req_5p-460.64 ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = -7 ft 1.296 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Remaining run-length difference for ramp layout option 2.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_020_Option_2" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                <dynexp formula="Length_req_5p" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Length_req_5p</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                 is the required horizontal sloping run at 5 percent. Subtract the 460.64 ft length entered for this layout option. A positive result means the option is short by that distance; a negative result means the entered option length exceeds the calculated run requirement.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="1 ft/0.05">
                <expbody>1 ft/0.05</expbody>
                <expresult> = 20 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Horizontal run needed for one vertical foot at a 5 percent slope.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_021_1_ft_0_05" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">Divide 1 ft of rise by 0.05 ft of rise per horizontal foot of run. Dividing by the slope converts the vertical distance into the required horizontal distance.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph />
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Elev_toEB2Ramp=47' 2 5/8&quot;">
                <expbody>Elev_toEB2Ramp=47' 2 5/8"</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Elevation at the upper end of the End Bent 2 ramp.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_022_Elev_toEB2Ramp" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This input is identified as coming from the pedestrian alignment in the 3D model. Use the same project elevation datum as the lower ramp elevation so their difference gives a real vertical drop.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Elev_boEB2Ramp = 24 ft 8 in">
                <expbody>Elev_boEB2Ramp = 24 ft 8 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Elevation at the lower end of the End Bent 2 ramp.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_023_Elev_boEB2Ramp" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is the entered lower endpoint elevation. It is subtracted from the upper endpoint elevation to determine how much height the sloping ramp must lose.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Elev_dropEB2ramp=Elev_toEB2Ramp-Elev_boEB2Ramp">
                <expbody>Elev_dropEB2ramp=Elev_toEB2Ramp-Elev_boEB2Ramp</expbody>
                <expresult> = 22 ft 6 5/8 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Vertical drop from the upper to the lower end of the End Bent 2 ramp.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_024_Elev_dropEB2ramp" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Subtract 
                <dynexp formula="Elev_boEB2Ramp" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_boEB2Ramp</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the lower endpoint elevation, from 
                <dynexp formula="Elev_toEB2Ramp" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_toEB2Ramp</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the upper endpoint elevation. The common datum cancels, leaving the height difference the ramp must accommodate.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="EB2_rampLength=20*Elev_dropEB2ramp">
                <expbody>EB2_rampLength=20*Elev_dropEB2ramp</expbody>
                <expresult> = 451 ft 0 1/2 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Horizontal run needed for the End Bent 2 ramp at 5 percent.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_025_EB2_rampLength" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                <dynexp formula="Elev_dropEB2ramp" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_dropEB2ramp</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                 is the required vertical drop. Multiply it by 20 because a 5 percent slope uses 20 horizontal feet for each vertical foot. This gives sloping-run plan length; no separate landing lengths are added in this expression.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Switchback_offramp_reqd = EB2_rampLength-(129.54'+138.54'+138.54')">
                <expbody>Switchback_offramp_reqd = EB2_rampLength-(129.54'+138.54'+138.54')</expbody>
                <expresult> = 44 ft 5 1/16 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Additional ramp run needed beyond the three entered End Bent 2 runs.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_026_Switchback_offramp_reqd" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" level="1">
                <dynexp formula="EB2_rampLength" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>EB2_rampLength</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                 is the total horizontal sloping run required. Add the three entered available run lengths inside the parentheses, then subtract that total from the required run.
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">A positive answer is the run still to provide in the switchback or off-ramp layout. A negative answer means the entered runs together are longer than this calculated requirement.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph />
        <paragraph>Scenario where we dont notch the noise wall and raise the alignment:</paragraph>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Current_clearance=6 3/8&quot;">
                <expbody>Current_clearance=6 3/8"</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Current gap used in the scenario that raises the alignment above the noise wall.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_027_Current_clearance" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is the measured or adopted vertical clearance before the alignment is raised. The following expression compares it with the target gap to find the additional height needed.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Req_Elev_Incrs=2ft-Current_clearance">
                <expbody>Req_Elev_Incrs=2ft-Current_clearance</expbody>
                <expresult> = 1 ft 5 5/8 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Additional elevation needed to reach the stated 2 ft clearance target.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_028_Req_Elev_Incrs" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Subtract 
                <dynexp formula="Current_clearance" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Current_clearance</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the gap already available, from the 2 ft target gap. A positive difference is how far the upper alignment must rise in this scenario, assuming the obstructing wall stays at the same elevation.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Elev_toEB2Ramp1 =  Elev_toEB2Ramp+Req_Elev_Incrs">
                <expbody>Elev_toEB2Ramp1 =  Elev_toEB2Ramp+Req_Elev_Incrs</expbody>
                <expresult> = 48 ft 8 1/4 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Upper ramp elevation after raising the alignment in the alternate scenario.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_029_Elev_toEB2Ramp1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Add 
                <dynexp formula="Req_Elev_Incrs" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Req_Elev_Incrs</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the required extra height, to 
                <dynexp formula="Elev_toEB2Ramp" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_toEB2Ramp</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the original upper ramp elevation. The suffix 1 identifies this raised-alignment scenario; the original input remains a separate value.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Elev_boEB2Ramp1 = 24 ft 8 in">
                <expbody>Elev_boEB2Ramp1 = 24 ft 8 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Lower ramp elevation entered for the raised-alignment scenario.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_030_Elev_boEB2Ramp1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is the lower endpoint for the alternate ramp geometry. The upper elevation changes in the preceding equation; this lower endpoint is independently entered here.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Elev_dropEB2ramp1 = Elev_toEB2Ramp1-Elev_boEB2Ramp1">
                <expbody>Elev_dropEB2ramp1 = Elev_toEB2Ramp1-Elev_boEB2Ramp1</expbody>
                <expresult> = 24 ft 0 1/4 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Vertical drop required by the raised-alignment ramp scenario.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_031_Elev_dropEB2ramp1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Subtract 
                <dynexp formula="Elev_boEB2Ramp1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_boEB2Ramp1</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the alternate lower endpoint, from 
                <dynexp formula="Elev_toEB2Ramp1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_toEB2Ramp1</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the alternate upper endpoint. The answer is the vertical distance the new ramp layout must descend.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="EB2_rampLength1 = 20*Elev_dropEB2ramp1">
                <expbody>EB2_rampLength1 = 20*Elev_dropEB2ramp1</expbody>
                <expresult> = 480 ft 5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Horizontal sloping run required after the upper alignment is raised.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_032_EB2_rampLength1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Multiply 
                <dynexp formula="Elev_dropEB2ramp1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Elev_dropEB2ramp1</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the revised vertical drop, by 20 horizontal feet per vertical foot. This uses the same 5 percent grade as the original scenario. It does not separately add landing lengths.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Switchback_offramp_reqd1 = EB2_rampLength1-(129.54 ft+138.54 ft+138.54 ft)">
                <expbody>Switchback_offramp_reqd1 = EB2_rampLength1-(129.54 ft+138.54 ft+138.54 ft)</expbody>
                <expresult> = 73 ft 9 9/16 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Additional run needed beyond the three entered runs in the raised-alignment scenario.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_PedBridge_033_Switchback_offramp_reqd1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Add the three available run lengths inside the parentheses. Subtract their sum from 
                <dynexp formula="EB2_rampLength1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>EB2_rampLength1</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the revised required horizontal sloping run. A positive result is additional run still needed; a negative result is extra length already available.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
